        <h2>Mobile &amp; Wireless Expert Witness — Wi-Fi, WLAN &amp; Mobile Device Technologies</h2>

        <div class="two-col-text-img">
          <div>
            <p>Dr. Tal Lavian serves as a mobile and wireless technology expert witness in patent litigation, PTAB inter partes review (IPR) proceedings, and ITC Section 337 investigations involving wireless communications. As a <a href="/communications-expert-witness/telecommunications-expert-witness/">telecommunications expert witness</a> and <a href="/communications-expert-witness/internet-expert-witness/">internet technology expert</a>, he applies 20 years of academic research at UC Berkeley and hands-on industry experience to mobile wireless technology analysis, combining deep technical knowledge with 90+ cases of patent litigation expertise.</p>

            <p>His background covers mobile wireless systems, devices, and networks. Dr. Lavian has experience with the relationships between wireless applications and their underlying <a href="/us-10348313-radar-target-detection-system/">communications</a> service architectures, designs, and implementations.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <img loading="lazy" src="/images/heroes/network-communications-expert.svg" alt="Network Communications Expert"  width="360" height="184"/>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Two-col: Wireless Network Protocols + Mobile & Wireless Expert -->
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <h3>Background</h3>

            <p>Dr. Lavian holds a Ph.D. in Computer Science from UC Berkeley, specializing in network communications, and spent 20 years researching, studying, and lecturing at UC Berkeley. He served as Principal Scientist and Principal Architect at Nortel Networks (1996&ndash;2007) and as a DARPA Principal Investigator. Dr. Lavian has over 120 <a href="/patents/">patents</a>, over 25 <a href="/scientific-publications/">scientific publications</a>, and has been retained in over 90 <a href="/cases-expert-witness-testimony/">cases</a>, including 60+ depositions, before U.S. federal courts, PTAB, ITC, and international tribunals, on behalf of over 50 law firms and corporate clients. His mobile and wireless case work includes <a href="/case/55-t-mobile-v-barkan-wireless-access-technologies/">T-Mobile v. Barkan Wireless Access Technologies</a> (U.S. Patent Nos. 8,559,369 and 9,042,306, involving wireless access technologies), <a href="/case/18-ixi-mobile-v-apple-inc/">IXI Mobile v. Apple</a> (U.S. Patent Nos. 7,426,398 and 7,295,532, involving mobile device technologies), and <a href="/cases-expert-witness-testimony/">Ericsson v. Samsung (ITC)</a> (U.S. Patent Nos. 6,772,215 and 6,519,223, involving wireless communications).</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Mobile &amp; Wireless Expert</h3>

            <p>The following are Dr. Tal Lavian&rsquo;s areas of expertise in Mobile and Wireless Technologies:</p>

            <ul>
              <li><a href="https://standards.ieee.org/ieee/802.11/5536/">Wi-Fi, IEEE 802.11,</a> MAC, PHY.</li>
              <li>Bluetooth, IEEE 802.15, short-range wireless protocols.</li>
              <li><a href="https://www.ietf.org/documents/149/95-802-11-Tutorial.pdf">Wireless LAN (WLAN)</a>, <a href="/communications-expert-witness/messaging-and-chat-expert-witness/">SMS, MMS</a>, Instant Messaging (IM) chat.</li>
              <li>ARQ and HARQ (Automatic Repeat reQuest / Hybrid ARQ) error control protocols.</li>
              <li>Handsets, mobile devices, smartphones.</li>
              <li>Wireless systems, architectures, and standards.</li>
              <li>Standards, systems, and backend infrastructure.</li>
            </ul>

            <p>Wireless <a href="/communications-expert-witness/telecommunications-expert-witness/">telecommunications</a> providers are experiencing growth in mobile data transmission, driving demand for mobile devices supporting data-intensive consumer-based applications, such as location-based services and 3D gaming. Mobile and wireless technologies and their associated infrastructure support applications such as defense, emergency response, logistics, smart city, <a href="/communications-expert-witness/data-communications-expert-witness/">network infrastructure</a>, and supply chain management.</p>

            <p>Mobile network infrastructure is based on a software-defined architecture that supports automation, configuration changes, and the addition of new capabilities.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>Mobile and Wireless in Patent Litigation</h2>

        <p>Dr. Lavian&rsquo;s mobile and wireless expertise covers Wi-Fi, wireless LAN protocols, wireless network access technologies, mobile device architectures, and <a href="/communications-expert-witness/network-security-expert-witness/">wireless security</a>. He provides analysis and testimony in patent disputes involving these technologies before U.S. federal courts, PTAB, and the ITC.</p>

        <section class="faq-section" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about mobile and wireless expert witness services">
          <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <details open>
            <summary>What wireless technologies is Dr. Lavian expert in?</summary>
            <p>Dr. Lavian is expert in Wi-Fi (IEEE 802.11), Bluetooth (IEEE 802.15), wireless LAN protocols, ARQ and HARQ error control protocols, mobile wireless network architecture, wireless access technologies, and mobile device networking in the context of patent litigation.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>Has Dr. Lavian testified in ITC wireless cases?</summary>
            <p>Yes. Dr. Lavian has testified in International Trade Commission (ITC) Section 337 investigations involving wireless communications technologies, including smartphones and wireless networking equipment.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>What is Dr. Lavian&rsquo;s background in wireless communications?</summary>
            <p>Dr. Lavian has a Ph.D. from UC Berkeley and research experience in wireless network protocols. His patent portfolio includes patents covering wireless communication technologies, and he has testified in wireless cases in federal courts, PTAB, and ITC proceedings.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>What types of wireless patent disputes has Dr. Lavian handled?</summary>
            <p>Dr. Lavian has handled patent disputes involving Wi-Fi implementations, wireless network access control, wireless roaming and handoff mechanisms, WLAN security, and mobile device connectivity architectures.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>What wireless companies has Dr. Lavian served as an expert for?</summary>
            <p>Dr. Lavian has been retained in wireless patent cases involving companies including Apple, Samsung, Motorola, T-Mobile, and Ericsson, providing analysis and testimony on Wi-Fi and wireless access technologies.</p>
          </details>
        </section>

